{"extract": "Qyrymbek Eleuūly Köşerbaev (Kazakh: Қырымбек Елеуұлы Көшербаев; born 20 May 1955) is a Kazakh politician who's serving as the State Secretary of Kazakhstan since 2019. Prior to that, Kusherbayev served as the head of the Presidential Administration, akim of Kyzylorda Region from 2013 to 2019, First Deputy Prime Minister of Kazakhstan from 2012 to 2013, akim of Mangystau Region from 2006 to 2011, Ambassador of Kazakhstan to Russia, Finland and Armenia from 2003 to 2006, akim of West Kazakhstan Region from 2000 to 2003, and the Minister of Education and Science from 1997 to 2000.", "links": [{"ns": 0, "title": "Academy of Sciences of the Soviet Union", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alma mater", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Altynbek Sarsenbayuly", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Bakhytzhan Sagintayev", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Bauyrzhan Mukhamedzhanov", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Communist Party of Kazakhstan (Soviet Union)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Darhan Kaletaev", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "East Slavic naming customs", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Erlan Karin", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Erlan Qoşanov", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Finland", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "First Deputy Prime Minister of Kazakhstan", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Imangali Tasmagambetov", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Jaqsylyq Dosqaliev", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kabibulla Dzhakupov", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kassym-Jomart Tokayev", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kazakh SSR", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kazakh language", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kazaly", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kyzylorda Region", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "List of Äkims of Kyzylorda Region", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "List of Äkims of Mangystau Region", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "List of Äkims of West Kaz